# MissionDeck — environment example
#
# MissionDeck reads plain process environment variables. It does NOT auto-load
# this file and has no dotenv dependency: export the variables in your shell, or
# copy this file to `.env` and load it with your own tooling. `.env` is ignored
# by Git and must never be committed.
#
# MISSIONDECK_ORCA_EXE
#   Absolute path to the Orca CLI.
#   Optional. When empty or unset, MissionDeck resolves `orca` from PATH.
#
#   Windows:
#   MISSIONDECK_ORCA_EXE=C:\Users\<you>\AppData\Local\Programs\Orca\resources\bin\orca.exe
#
#   macOS / Linux:
#   MISSIONDECK_ORCA_EXE=/usr/local/bin/orca
#
# There are no API keys, tokens, or credentials in this project. MissionDeck
# never stores provider credentials; it delegates all inference to the locally
# installed Orca runtime under that runtime's own account.
MISSIONDECK_ORCA_EXE=
